] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186513913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514305 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a8e47ae0-7d67-5cf0-9030-1e73b5fe057a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(yz)$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc4d5cf2-890e-5aaa-adb5-f60e0888df55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514463 #edb/ref 1074 "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(yz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(yz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(yz))\\,k \\\\  & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i+(-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(yz))\\text{ }j+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(yz)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0) & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(-(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+0\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0))\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i-j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i-j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2},0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514494 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514494 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2c774462-5887-556e-8c1c-42d4884f6cfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514494 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514514 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514514 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a1f6e0c-4f5f-50c7-b0d9-d452532aced4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514514 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514523 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9a38a9f-1171-55bf-a06a-39b676731e34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514523 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186266053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514537 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514537 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d0f5d1fa-3cf9-5f94-8815-62bf015679e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514537 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514547 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514547 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f9ae40c4-6ef1-5389-b6b7-49816af3ef18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514547 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265960 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
